A minimalist version of vi(1).  It is an example of the "Buffer Gap"
method outlined in the The Craft Of Text Editing used by many Emacs
style editors.

Create or read a text file to edit.  Text files consists of lines of
printable UTF-8 text, tabs, or newline characters.  A physical line
can be of arbitrary length and is delimited by either a newline or the
end of file.  Tab stops are every eight columns.  The behaviour of
non-printable characters may vary depending on the implementation of
the Curses library, stty(1) settings, or terminal emulator.
